  "id": "COMPOUND:2628 - PROTEIN:558",
  "verbalization": "Pregnenolone is implicated in the target pathway leading to 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Pregnenolone acts as a target of the Liver X receptor (LXR), which in turn is targeted by two distinct compounds: 2-[(4S)-4-hydroxy-3,6-dioxodioxan-4-yl]acetic acid and 5-Alpha-Androstane-3-Beta,17beta-Diol. Both of these compounds are known to interact with 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase, indicating a shared mechanism of action. The presence of multiple pathways involving different ligands targeting the same enzyme suggests a potential role for Pregnenolone in modulating the activity of these ligands, possibly through a common downstream effect on 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the regulatory network, where Pregnenolone may influence the activity of the Liver X receptor, thereby affecting the downstream targets of its ligands. This interconnectedness underscores the importance of understanding the broader context of Pregnenolone's role in drug-target relationships.",
